Package: CorOncoEndpoints
Type: Package
Title: Correlated Progression-Free Survival, Overall Survival and Objective
    Response for Oncology Trial Simulation
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Gosuke",
                  family = "Homma",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com")
Description: Generates correlated progression-free survival (PFS), overall
    survival (OS) and binary objective response for oncology clinical trial
    simulations. PFS is exactly exponential and the response probability
    equals the specified objective response rate; PFS and response are linked
    through a Gaussian copula. OS follows an illness-death structure in which
    the death hazard after progression can differ from the death hazard before
    progression and can depend on response (Fleischer et al. (2009)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.3637>; Meller et al. (2019) <doi:10.1002/sim.8295>), or,
    alternatively, both PFS and OS are exactly exponential. The generator is
    calibrated to design inputs such as medians, the response rate and the
    association between PFS and response, and further functions compute the
    implied correlations, survival functions, expected numbers of events,
    average hazard ratios and the number of events required by the log-rank
    test. A group can also be described by two of the three endpoints, and the
    correlation between PFS and OS can be given instead of the proportion of
    PFS events that are deaths. Trials are simulated with piecewise accrual
    given by rates or proportions, exponential or piecewise exponential
    dropout and censoring of PFS alone. Random numbers are generated with
    'dqrng' and transformed in 'C++' via 'Rcpp'.
